WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
Listen closely to these two:

2
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.290
«je jouerai», «je jouais».

3
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.080
They look like near twins.

4
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.420
But one means 'I will play'.

5
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.870
The other means 'I used to play'.

6
00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.080
And there's no separate word
for 'will' in either one.

7
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.480
So which is which?

8
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.870
And how can French say 'I will' with no

9
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.790
word for 'will' at all?

10
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.330
In this mission, you'll follow three
different roads into the future,

11
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.650
and compare them.

12
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.600
Then you'll snap verb
pieces together in the lab,

13
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.050
predict first, and build
future forms of your own.

14
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.870
Your mission: find out
how French can say 'I

15
00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.360
will' without any word for 'will'.
